ial they took from  mar-a-lago that they won't put things in  those boxes to entrap him how do we know  their lawyers weren't allowed to see the  boxes go they weren't categorized  thousands of documents were taken well  rand  is there any  reason to believe  that such a thing was done because for  everybody mentioning the planting of  evidence  no one has been able to present any  actual reason to believe that that  happened how do we know that they're  going to be honest with us about what's  actually in the boxes how do we know  that was in the box before it left the  residence if the lawyers weren't allowed  to see everything so you know they've  lost a great deal of trust and it's uh  yeah so there's rand paul asserting it  and this is sort of the anatomy of a  conspiracy theory it will often start  sort of quietly as an aside with the  most partisan people trump's lawyers for  example going listen it wouldn't shock  me if they even planted evidence oh yeah  yeah yeah  and then people like fox news hosts  start uh latching onto it and we played  a number of examples of that from  yesterday and next thing you know  sitting senators and sitting members of  congress are doing the same thing it  almost seemed like marjorie taylor green  got it from an oan host here is marjorie  taylor green yesterday nodding along as  an oan host says maybe evidence was  planted and then i'll show you how later  in the day she makes it her own in all  of the all of the documents and  everything president trump had at  mar-a-lago that isn't anything that the  fbi needed to raid his home for that is  no we already talked about that earlier  the gsa approved it the the the gsa  approved the documents mailed them  sealed them and sent them to him so why  would the government give them to him  for now the government to come take them  back that's completely untrue by the way  but that's not the focus today unless  they're planting something anyway i  gotta switch back because we're  literally almost out of time words i  knew this would happen because you and i  are so marjorie taylor green saying  about they unless they plan to plant  evidence yeah  and right and then later in the day  marjorie taylor green going full-fledged  in on this tweeting quote  i think now look at the language right i  think so that's your that's your  thinking you don't have evidence i think  that there is an extremely high  probability  that the fbi planted evidence against  president trump otherwise why would they  not allow his attorneys or anyone watch  them while they conducted their  unprecedented raid  they know the consequences of an  empty-handed power move  this rings completely and totally hollow  it just doesn't pass the sniff test and  let me also talk a little bit about  marjorie taylor green's use of the word  unprecedented yesterday  um  we talked about marsha blackburn's  comment  if they can do this to trump they can do  this to anyone to which we said they  already do it to anyone the question is  will they ever do it to people in  positions of power the other one that  trump and others have been talking about  is that this was an unprecedented raid  first of all i you know i've been guilty  of this as well  the fbi doesn't really do raids i mean  this wasn't really a raid  they had a search warrant and they  served it that that's what that's what  it was it was a search warrant they  executed a search warrant so the use of  raid it's colloquially used and i do it  as well but understand that this this  was they served a search warrant  unprecedented is a big focus for them  trump said no this has never happened to  any president before  and now a lot of these right-wingers  have latched on to the idea of  unprecedented well if it's never been  done before then it must be wrong  we've never had a president who did the  things that donald trump did  so it's logical that i mean sort of like  a mathematical equation when you have  unique inputs you will have a unique  output and we're starting with the  president who did things no other  president has done it's logical it would  be to be expected that the outcomes also  are unlike those that we have seen  before and one such outcome is indeed a  search warrant being served by the fbi  on donald trump's home there is no  evidence that they planted evidence if  we ever learned that the fbi planted  evidence i will tell you that  and i will absolutely condemn it for now  there's no reason to think that that  took place
 

